# `check` audits the belief store itself.
#
# Every question so far has been about one name. This one is about the whole
# brain: what is unsourced, what has gone stale, what is contested, and what
# rests on something that no longer exists.
#
# A retrieval system has no equivalent. There is no query you can send a
# vector index that means "tell me which of your contents contradict each
# other," because the index has no notion of two chunks being about the same
# fact, let alone disagreeing about it.

now is 2026-09-04T12:00:00Z

trust legal above compliance above policy above staff above user above rumor

# Healthy: sourced, current, uncontested.
company.name is "Acme" as legal from certificate_of_incorporation

# Unsourced: nobody can say where this came from.
company.headcount is 240 as policy

# Stale: the lifetime ran out in January and nothing renewed it.
company.insurance_policy is "AXA-88213" as compliance from broker_email on 2025-01-01 for 1 year

# Contested: two policy documents, same stated day, different answers.
company.fiscal_year_end is "12-31" as policy from finance_handbook on 2026-02-01
company.fiscal_year_end is "03-31" as policy from tax_filing on 2026-02-01

# Refused: an override that never had the standing to land.
company.name is "Acme Holdings" as user from support_ticket

# Orphaned: this rests on an episode nobody ever wrote down.
company.status is "under_review" as compliance from regulator_letter because sec_inquiry

show "Health of the brain:"
